sp("about","About PorchMath","About PorchMath: free home improvement material calculators.","<p>PorchMath is a free collection of material calculators for homeowners and DIYers. Each tool shows the formula it uses, a worked example and practical tips, so you can understand—and double-check—every estimate.</p><h2 id='how'>How we build our calculators</h2><p>Formulas are standard geometry (area and volume) combined with typical material data such as bag yields, coverage rates and densities. Where numbers vary by product, the calculator lets you enter the value from your product label.</p><h2>Accuracy</h2><p>Results are estimates. Always confirm quantities with your supplier and follow local building codes and manufacturer instructions.</p>")
sp("privacy","Privacy Policy","PorchMath privacy policy.","<p><i>Last updated: October 29, 2026</i></p><p>PorchMath calculators run entirely in your browser. The numbers you enter are not sent to or stored on our servers.</p><h2>Hosting and logs</h2><p>The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, which may process technical data such as IP addresses for security and performance, as described in Cloudflare's privacy policy.</p><h2>Cookies and advertising</h2><p>We do not currently set cookies. In the future we may show ads (for example via Google AdSense). Third-party vendors, including Google, may then use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits. You can opt out of personalized advertising at <a href='https://adssettings.google.com'>Google Ads Settings</a> or <a href='https://www.aboutads.info'>aboutads.info</a>. This policy will be updated before any such service is enabled.</p><h2>Affiliate links</h2><p>Some pages may in future contain affiliate links (for example Amazon Associates). As an Amazon Associate we would earn from qualifying purchases, at no extra cost to you. Affiliate links will be clearly disclosed.</p><h2>Anonymous usage counts</h2><p>To learn which tools are actually used, the site sends a tiny anonymous signal when you use a tool, for example when you press Calculate, choose a file, finish processing or download a result. The signal contains only the tool name, the type of action, the page language, your country as reported by Cloudflare and your browser family (such as Chrome). It never includes your files, text or the values you enter. Actions counted are: Calculate (including the first valid live result on a page), choose a file, finish processing, download and copy. Each count is stored with the date only (no time of day). We set no cookies, use no identifiers and do not store your IP address. To block abuse, the server keeps a salted one-way hash of your IP address and the current minute for at most a few minutes, then deletes it.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about this policy: email <a href='mailto:Duylinh30190@gmail.com'>Duylinh30190@gmail.com</a> or see our <a href='/contact/'>Contact page</a>.</p>")
sp("contact","Contact","Contact PorchMath.","<p>Found a bug, a wrong number, or want a new calculator? We'd love to hear from you.</p><p>Email: <a href='mailto:Duylinh30190@gmail.com'>Duylinh30190@gmail.com</a></p><p>You can also <a href='https://github.com/yamakaru/porchmath/issues'>open an issue on GitHub</a>.</p>")
